# Pinned upstream revisions. realmctl and CI read this file; the Dockerfiles take
# them as build-args. Bump deliberately and rebuild the images.
MANGOS_CLASSIC_COMMIT=de8f72993b9e1faa1bf92dd5505f3daec5cea3ce
CLASSIC_DB_COMMIT=4d230bb1bd477948cac61c107d2718b3ea04a5b8
# github.com/cmangos/playerbots, dropped into src/modules/PlayerBots; moves with the core pin.
PLAYERBOTS_COMMIT=31e0f32b543fee46941db51225bb7b432eace236
WENILLA_REPO=https://github.com/Arnesen/wenilla
# A full commit hash, never a branch name — branch names are not reproducible builds.
# This is the head of wenilla's `main`, and `bump-realm-pin.yml` over there rewrites the line
# below on every push to it. That is now the correct behaviour, because every carry lives on
# `main`: the browser port itself, the JavaScript bridge (Arnesen/wenilla#16), and the zone
# soundscape fix (Arnesen/wenilla#14) that keeps a zone line or doorway from freezing the frame
# for ~200 ms. Upstream (samwhosung/benilla) is merged into `main` as ordinary commits, so
# "pin = main's head" and "we are current with upstream, carries included" are the same claim.
#
# It was not always so. #14 sat unmerged on a side branch on the theory that upstream syncing
# force-resets `main`, and the pin was hand-set to that branch — which the workflow then
# overwrote on every push to `main`, three times (f41fa747 -> 52b0c45 -> 46a1fd9c -> bf1be553),
# silently dropping the soundscape fix each time while this comment claimed otherwise. Syncing
# does not force-reset anything: the sync commits are ordinary commits on `main`. The one
# force-reset came from GitHub's "Sync fork" button, whose "discard commits" path hard-resets a
# diverged fork. Sync through the `sync-upstream` PR flow, never that button.
#
# So: do not hand-edit the line below to something off `main` — the workflow will overwrite it
# and the fix will be silent. Land the change on wenilla `main` instead and let the pin follow.
WENILLA_COMMIT=db151ec4b06e267717d9fe2816d7b4d4951366de
